from pathlib import Path
from runpy import run_path
g=run_path(str(Path(__file__).with_name('author-tools-generator.py')))
L=g['lesson']; C=g['course']

aws=[
('What AWS provides','Amazon Web Services offers rented computing and storage. You choose services for a job and pay according to their rules and usage.','Need: share a static reading page\nPossible parts: object storage and a content delivery service\nPractice today: draw the plan only','A static page does not need a running application server just because it is hosted in the cloud.','List which files a static page needs.','Cloud resources can cost money even while you are learning; this course creates none.','Does a static page always need an application server?','No','Yes'),
('Regions and Availability Zones','An AWS Region is a geographic area. It contains separate Availability Zones designed to reduce shared failure risks.','Region: eu-west-1\nAvailability Zone: eu-west-1a\nPlan: keep related practice resources in a chosen Region','The Region and Zone names describe different levels of location. Zone letter mappings can differ between accounts.','Draw a Region containing more than one Zone.','Do not assume two Zones are the same physical building.','Which level contains Availability Zones?','A Region','A storage object'),
('Identity and access with IAM','IAM controls who can do what in AWS. A policy grants actions on resources. Least privilege means granting only needed actions.','Reader needs: read one approved object\nReader does not need: change account settings or delete a bucket','A small permission scope limits mistakes. A real policy must name the intended actions and resources.','Describe the minimum job of a read-only reviewer.','Do not practise with root-account access or put credentials in source files.','What should an access policy grant?','Only the needed access','Every possible action'),
('S3 objects and buckets','Amazon S3 stores objects inside buckets. An object has a key, which is its name within a bucket. Slashes in keys can look like folders.','Bucket: fictional-club-assets\nObject key: pages/index.html\nObject data: the page file','The bucket groups objects; the key identifies one object. Bucket names follow service-wide naming rules.','Choose a key for a logo file.','Do not make a bucket public just to work around an access error.','What identifies an object inside a bucket?','Its key','Only its file color'),
('Object access and versioning','S3 access settings decide who can read an object. Versioning can retain earlier versions, but it is separate from access control and backup planning.','Object: pages/index.html\nVersion A: old heading\nVersion B: corrected heading\nAccess: remains controlled separately','Keeping versions can help recover an earlier file. It can also use extra storage.','Explain why versions should not contain real secrets.','Turning on versioning does not make an object private automatically.','Does versioning replace access control?','No','Yes'),
('EC2 virtual machines','An EC2 instance is a virtual machine. You choose its size and operating-system image, then remain responsible for much of its software upkeep.','Planned instance: small Linux VM\nJob: a separate learning experiment\nNeeded upkeep: updates, permissions and monitoring','The machine is more flexible than simple object storage, but it brings more maintenance and cost.','Name one task that does not need a VM.','Stopping a VM may not remove charges for associated storage or other resources.','What is an EC2 instance?','A virtual machine','A single S3 object'),
('VPCs and subnets','A Virtual Private Cloud is a network space you configure. A subnet is a range of network addresses inside that VPC and one Availability Zone.','VPC range: 10.0.0.0/16\nExample subnet: 10.0.1.0/24\nLocation: one chosen Availability Zone','The subnet is a smaller address range within the VPC. The numbers are a planning example, not a command.','Draw two non-overlapping subnets.','Do not overlap address ranges without understanding the network consequences.','Where is a subnet placed?','Inside a VPC and one Availability Zone','Across every AWS Region'),
('Security groups filter traffic','A security group controls allowed traffic for attached resources. It is stateful: replies to allowed traffic are handled as part of that connection.','Example web rule: allow TCP 443 from the intended clients\nNo rule: unrestricted administration from the whole internet','The web rule describes HTTPS traffic. Administrative access should be much more restricted.','Explain why a practice server should not expose every port.','A security group is not a substitute for patching software and checking application permissions.','Which port commonly carries HTTPS?','443','22'),
('CloudFront caches content','CloudFront is a content delivery service. It can serve cached copies from edge locations nearer to visitors.','Visitor -> nearby edge cache\nCache miss -> approved origin\nResponse -> visitor','A cache hit can avoid another trip to the origin. Cache rules determine how updates become visible.','Choose whether a logo or a private account page should be freely cached.','Do not cache private personalised data with public cache rules.','What happens on a cache miss?','The service may fetch from the origin','The original file is deleted'),
('CloudWatch observations','CloudWatch provides metrics, logs and alarms for supported resources. A metric is a number over time; an alarm checks a condition.','Metric: request errors per minute\nAlarm condition: errors exceed the chosen threshold\nResponse plan: inspect logs and recent changes','The alarm points to a problem to investigate. It does not explain the cause by itself.','Write a non-secret log line for a failed page request.','Do not collect unnecessary personal data in logs.','What does an alarm check?','A configured condition','Every possible bug'),
('Budgets are alerts','A budget helps track spending and can notify you when a threshold is reached. An alert is not automatically a hard spending stop.','Monthly learning limit: a fictional 5 currency units\nAlert threshold: 80 percent\nAlert point: 4 units','The arithmetic is 5 times 0.8. These are invented planning numbers, not an AWS price quote.','Calculate a 50 percent alert point for the same budget.','Read service costs and clean up authorised practice resources; an alert alone does not cap charges.','Does an alert always stop spending?','No','Yes'),
('Plan a static site carefully','A cloud design should name the needed services, access rules, costs and cleanup steps. Keep a static learning site as static files.','Files: HTML, CSS, JavaScript and images\nAccess: read-only delivery to visitors\nOrigin: approved static-file storage\nReview: domain, HTTPS, cache rules, cost','This is a deployment plan only. It introduces no user database or login backend.','Identify which part would change after updating a CSS file.','Do not deploy a plan until the owner approves the exact resources and cost.','What does this static site require?','Static files and delivery configuration','A mandatory login database'),
]
C('aws','AWS offers cloud computing, storage and networking services. Learn the names of the main parts, read a simple static-site plan and understand access and cost before creating anything.','All examples are read-only worked plans. No AWS account, card, keys or deployed resources are needed to learn here. A real deployment is a separate authorised task.','https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/aws-overview/introduction.html',[L(*r) for r in aws])

azure=[
('Meet the Azure cloud','Microsoft Azure offers rented services for computing, storage and networking. A useful design begins with the job, not with the longest list of services.','Goal: publish a small static club page\nInputs: HTML, CSS and image files\nDecision: choose a static-file hosting option','The page files can be delivered without creating an account system for visitors.','List which parts of a school page are static.','Creating real cloud resources can incur charges; these lessons only describe them.','What should come before choosing services?','The goal','A large shopping list of resources'),
('Subscriptions and resource groups','An Azure subscription is a billing and management boundary. A resource group collects related resources for a project.','Subscription: approved learning subscription\nResource group: rg-club-practice\nResources: storage and monitoring for the club project','The group gives related resources a shared management container. Resource-level settings still matter.','Name a group for a separate fictional project.','Deleting a resource group deletes its contained resources; never do that to an unknown group.','What groups related Azure resources?','A resource group','A browser bookmark'),
('Regions and availability','An Azure region is a geographic area. Many regions offer availability zones, which provide separate physical locations within the region.','Choose a supported region\nCheck whether the chosen service supports zones there\nPlan copies if the availability need justifies them','Service features vary by region. A region name alone does not guarantee every feature is available.','Explain why location can affect waiting time for visitors.','Check the service\'s current regional support before planning a zonal feature.','Should regional feature support be checked?','Yes','No'),
('Microsoft Entra identities','Microsoft Entra ID manages identities. An identity can represent a person, application or workload, depending on how access is arranged.','Person identity: a reviewer\nWorkload identity: an approved application\nAccess decision: assign only the required role at the right scope','Identity answers who is asking. A permission assignment answers what that identity may do.','Explain the difference between identity and permission.','Do not share one personal account among many learners.','What does identity describe?','Who or what is asking','The file size'),
('Azure role assignments','Azure role-based access control assigns a role to an identity at a scope. Scope can be a resource, resource group or broader boundary.','Identity: fictional reviewer\nRole: Reader\nScope: rg-club-practice','The reviewer can inspect resources at that scope without getting general edit permission from this assignment.','Compare a resource scope with a whole subscription scope.','A broad scope can grant more access than intended.','What does scope decide?','Where a role assignment applies','The user\'s screen size'),
('Blob Storage containers','Azure Blob Storage keeps objects called blobs. Containers group blobs inside a storage account.','Storage account -> container club-files\nContainer -> blob images/logo.png','The account, container and blob are three different levels. The blob name can contain slashes.','Choose a blob name for index.html.','Public read access should be an explicit decision, not a fix for every permission error.','What is stored inside a container?','Blobs','Subscriptions'),
('Static website files','An Azure Storage static website uses an index document and an error document. It is a way to serve files, not an application backend.','Index document: index.html\nError document: 404.html\nContent: compiled frontend files','The index opens the site; the error document helps when a page is missing. A real site also needs correct routing and domain configuration.','Explain why asset paths must work after uploading.','Static website access has different settings from ordinary private blob access; check the official service guide.','What does static hosting execute on the server?','No custom application backend','Every browser JavaScript file as a server program'),
('Virtual machines need upkeep','An Azure virtual machine is a configurable computer in the cloud. Its operating system and software still need care.','Planned VM: one Linux practice machine\nOwner tasks: updates, accounts, disk care and monitoring','A VM may be useful for a separate experiment, but it is unnecessary for many static pages.','Compare the maintenance needed by a VM and a static-file site.','Deleting or stopping one resource may leave related disks or addresses with their own costs.','Who must plan VM software upkeep?','The resource owner','The browser visitor'),
('Virtual networks and subnets','A virtual network provides a private network space. Subnets divide that space into smaller address ranges for resources.','VNet: 10.2.0.0/16\nSubnet web: 10.2.1.0/24\nSubnet tools: 10.2.2.0/24','The example subnet ranges are separate. Network routes and access rules decide how traffic moves.','Draw which resources would belong in each subnet.','Do not confuse an address range with a permission to access a service.','What does a subnet divide?','Network address space','A subscription bill equally'),
('Network security groups','A network security group contains rules that allow or deny network traffic. Rules have priorities, so their order matters.','Rule priority 100: allow approved HTTPS traffic\nLater rules: handle other traffic according to the plan','A smaller priority number is processed before a larger one. The full rule set determines the result.','Write a plan that keeps administration restricted to approved sources.','Do not open every port to the internet to make troubleshooting easier.','Which rule priority is considered earlier?','100 before 200','200 before 100'),
('Azure Monitor helps you observe','Azure Monitor collects supported metrics and logs. Alerts can tell you when a chosen condition is met.','Metric: failed requests\nAlert: more failures than the agreed threshold\nInvestigation: compare logs and recent changes','The alert calls attention to a symptom. Someone still needs to find and fix its cause.','Choose an alert that is useful for a static page.','Collect only the information needed for the task, especially on sites used by children.','Does an alert explain every cause automatically?','No','Yes'),
('Cost planning and cleanup','Azure budgets can notify you about spending. Review actual resource costs and plan cleanup; notifications are not a general guarantee that spending stops.','Fictional budget: 10 units\nAlert at 80 percent: 8 units\nCleanup list: only resources created for this approved practice','These numbers teach a budget calculation, not a real service price.','List related resources that should be checked before ending a VM experiment.','Never delete a shared resource group as casual cleanup.','What must cleanup target?','Only the authorised practice resources','Every visible resource group'),
]
C('azure','Azure provides cloud services from Microsoft. Learn subscriptions, resource groups, identities, storage and networking with small worked plans and no real deployment.','No Azure account or payment details are needed to read this course. Examples describe fictional resources. Creating or changing real resources is a separate authorised activity.','https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cloud-adoption-framework/ready/azure-setup-guide/',[L(*r) for r in azure])

google=[
('Meet Google Cloud','Google Cloud provides hosted services for computing, storage and data work. Begin by matching a service to a small, clear need.','Need: store the files for a club page\nData: index.html, styles.css and logo.png\nNo need: visitor passwords or a custom database','The example is a static-file problem. Cloud hosting does not force the app to have a backend.','Separate static files from a feature that would need live server work.','Cloud experiments may have costs; no resources are created by these lessons.','Does cloud hosting force a login backend?','No','Yes'),
('Projects organise resources','A Google Cloud project groups resources and settings. It has a project name, a project ID and a project number with different roles.','Display name: Club practice\nProject ID: fictional-club-practice\nProject number: assigned by the service','The display name is for people; the ID is used by many tools and APIs. This is a fictional planning example.','Explain why you should check the active project before any command.','A familiar display name is not enough to prove you selected the right project.','Which identifier do many commands use?','Project ID','Only the display color'),
('Regions and zones','A region is a geographic area. A zone is a deployment area within a region. Some resources are zonal, regional or global.','Region example: us-central1\nZone example: us-central1-a\nPlan: check the location type of each service','The correct location field depends on the resource. A VM and an object-storage bucket do not use location settings in exactly the same way.','Classify a planned VM as a zonal resource.','Do not assume every service uses a zone field.','What contains zones?','A region','An individual VM'),
('IAM roles and principals','A principal is an identity asking for access. An IAM role groups permissions, and a policy binds a role to principals at a resource scope.','Principal: fictional reviewer\nRole: an appropriate read-only role\nScope: the intended practice resource','The design gives a specific reader limited access. Choose the actual predefined role from the service guide.','Explain why broad basic roles may grant more than a reviewer needs.','Do not grant owner access merely to bypass a permission error.','What does a role group?','Permissions','File extensions'),
('Service accounts are workload identities','A service account represents an application or workload. It is different from a person\'s user account.','Workload: approved report task\nIdentity: its own service account\nAccess: only the data needed for the report','A separate identity makes the workload\'s access easier to limit and review.','Describe what access a read-only report needs.','Avoid downloading long-lived keys when a supported keyless identity method fits the task.','Who does a service account represent?','A workload','Every visitor to a site'),
('Cloud Storage objects','Cloud Storage keeps objects in buckets. An object name identifies the object within its bucket.','Bucket: fictional-club-files\nObject name: images/logo.png\nData: the logo file','The bucket groups objects. A slash in the object name is useful organisation, not a requirement for a real folder.','Choose an object name for a stylesheet.','Decide access rules deliberately before making any object public.','What identifies the logo inside the bucket?','Its object name','Its screen position'),
('Object versions and lifecycle rules','Versioning and lifecycle rules can help retain or clean up object versions. They need a deliberate policy so useful data is not lost or kept forever.','Keep current page files\nRetain older versions for an agreed recovery period\nReview lifecycle cleanup rules before enabling them','The policy balances recovery and storage use. Actual rule syntax depends on the service configuration.','Explain which files need longer recovery time.','A cleanup rule can delete data; inspect its scope before use.','What must be reviewed before lifecycle cleanup?','The rule\'s target and effect','Only the bucket icon'),
('Compute Engine virtual machines','Compute Engine provides virtual machines. You choose a machine configuration, image and location and manage the guest software.','Planned VM: one small learning instance\nImage: a supported operating system\nOwner work: patching, access and monitoring','The VM is a rented computer, not a zero-maintenance static-file bucket.','Name a task better served by static file hosting.','Stopping a VM does not necessarily remove charges for associated disks.','What is a Compute Engine instance?','A virtual machine','A single JSON field'),
('VPC networks and subnets','Google Cloud VPC networks are global resources. Their subnets are regional. This is a useful distinction from some other cloud network models.','VPC: club-network\nSubnet: club-subnet in us-central1\nAddress range: 10.3.1.0/24','The network can contain regional subnets. A subnet\'s addresses and region matter when attaching resources.','Draw a second subnet in a different region.','Do not assume a VPC network itself belongs to just one region.','Which resource is regional here?','The subnet','The VPC network'),
('Firewall rules control connections','VPC firewall rules allow or deny selected traffic for targeted resources. A good rule names the needed sources, protocol and ports.','Target: intended practice web VM\nAllowed: HTTPS on TCP 443 from approved sources\nAdministration: restricted separately','The rule describes a narrow purpose. It should not open every port just because the machine is a test machine.','Explain why source ranges should be reviewed.','A firewall rule cannot fix an insecure application by itself.','What should an allow rule include?','Only required traffic','Every port and source'),
('Logging and Monitoring','Cloud Logging records supported events. Cloud Monitoring tracks metrics and alert conditions. Use both to understand a problem.','Metric: failed requests per minute\nLog event: one request could not find a file\nAction: check the file path and deployment contents','The metric shows a pattern; the log explains one event.','Write a useful missing-file message without personal data.','Do not log tokens or private messages to make diagnosis easier.','Which service records event details?','Cloud Logging','A billing label'),
('Budgets and labels','Budgets help monitor spend and send notifications. Labels help group costs by project purpose. Neither is a reason to skip cost review.','Label: purpose=learning\nFictional monthly budget: 6 units\nAlert at half: 3 units','The label helps organise the resources; the alert threshold is 3 units. These are invented numbers.','Calculate an 80 percent threshold for 10 units.','Budget alerts do not automatically stop all Google Cloud spending.','Does a budget alert guarantee a spending stop?','No','Yes'),
]
C('google-cloud','Google Cloud offers projects, storage, virtual machines and network tools. Learn the main ideas through fictional plans and simple checks before considering any real resources.','You need no Google Cloud account, card or keys to read these lessons. Examples are worked plans only. Real resource changes need separate permission and cost review.','https://cloud.google.com/docs/overview',[L(*r) for r in google])
